.Dd $Mdocdate: November 13 2026 $
.Dt VMDTRAY 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vmdtray
.Nd traffic light for vmd virtual machines in the system tray
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm vmdtray
.Op Fl c Ar console
.Op Fl i Ar interval
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
docks into the system tray of the X11 desktop and shows the state of the
.Xr vmd 8
virtual machines as a traffic light.
Every
.Ar interval
seconds it runs
.Dq Nm vmctl Cm status
and lights one lamp:
.Bl -tag -width "yellow"
.It green
Every virtual machine is running.
.It yellow
Some virtual machines are running and others are not, or one is stopping,
paused or waiting.
.It red
No virtual machine is running, none is configured, or
.Xr vmd 8
cannot be reached.
.El
.Pp
The window title, which the tray may show as a tooltip, tells how many
virtual machines are running.
Clicking the traffic light with the left mouse button starts the virtual
machine manager in its own session.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c Ar console
Run
.Ar console
when the traffic light is clicked.
It must be an absolute path.
The default is
.Pa /usr/local/bin/vmConsola .
.It Fl i Ar interval
Check the virtual machines every
.Ar interval
seconds, from 1 to 3600.
The default is 5.
.El
.Pp
.Nm
needs a system tray that implements the freedesktop.org system tray
protocol over XEmbed.
On desktops whose tray only speaks StatusNotifierItem, such as KDE Plasma,
the xembedsniproxy daemon bridges the two.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/usr/local/bin/vmConsola" -compact
.It Pa /usr/sbin/vmctl
queried for the state of the virtual machines
.It Pa /usr/local/bin/vmConsola
default virtual machine manager
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
runs until it is killed or the X server goes away, and exits >0 if an
error occurs.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vm.conf 5 ,
.Xr vmctl 8 ,
.Xr vmd 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Leonardo Santagostini Aq Mt leonardo@santagostini.com.ar
